"// @@@ Every element up to and including the modified index remains unchanged after the operation."

We are inside method insertElementAt(E obj, int index). It inserts obj at index, shifting elements from index onward right by one. The comment says: every element up to and including the modified index remains unchanged after the operation. Wait "up to and including the modified index" - after insertion, the element at position index is the new obj, so the original element at index should have moved to index+1, thus the element at index after operation is new obj, not unchanged. But maybe they mean elements before index (i.e., up to index-1) remain unchanged. However phrase says "up to and including the modified index". Might be a mistake; but we follow comment.

