Thus we assert: for all int i; 0 <= i && i <= index; this.elementAt(i).equals(\old(this.elementAt(i)));

But we need to use public observer methods. We have elementAt(int index) method (synchronized) which returns element at index. So we can use this.elementAt(i).equals(\old(this.elementAt(i))). Use .equals for objects.

Thus final assert:

assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i <= index; this.elementAt(i).equals(\old(this.elementAt(i)));

